{
  "id": "ss.char.blok",
  "name": "Blok",
  "description": "A survivor that put on everything it could find. The heaviest plating of the eight: a square helmet, square shoulders under two pauldrons, a riveted chest plate with the seam still on it — the block it used to be, worn as armour — and a pair of beetle elytra closed over its back like a shell it never opens. Limbs a third thicker than the rest, and it stands wide, which is what the weight costs. Spore pods are the weapon that suits a thing this slow: one racked on the back, one hung at the hip, both with the cold fuse the pod always carries, because in this world a warm glow is a thing calling to the hive. Same dead organ as the rest, same place. Bare chitin cold slate, gold plate over it. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
